WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:07.467
Darkness seemed to swim around me as I sat at a table in my room, resting my head on my arms.

2
00:00:07.468 --> 00:00:16.471
Mr. Rochester was not what I had thought him to be. I knew I must leave him, but I had no strength to flee.

3
00:00:16.472 --> 00:00:22.946
Late in the afternoon I raised my head. "What am I to do?" I asked myself.

4
00:00:22.947 --> 00:00:29.874
But the answer that came to mind—leave Thornfield—was so dreadful that I couldn't bear it.

5
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:36.794
I stood up and my head spun. Then I remembered that I hadn't eaten anything since breakfast.

6
00:00:36.795 --> 00:00:43.532
I opened my door and stumbled over Mr. Rochester, who was sitting in a chair at my threshold.

7
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:50.814
"You shut yourself up and grieve alone," he said. "I would prefer you come out and shout at me."

8
00:00:50.815 --> 00:00:54.839
I said nothing but regarded him wearily.

9
00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.407
"Jane, I never meant to wound you. Will you ever forgive me?"

10
00:01:00.407 --> 00:01:03.610
Reader, I forgave him on the spot.

11
00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:14.964
There was such deep remorse in his eye, such pity in his voice, and such unchanged love in his manner. I forgave him all but did not tell him so.

12
00:01:14.965 --> 00:01:22.399
"You know I'm a scoundrel, Jane?" he inquired. I suppose he wondered at my continued silence.

13
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.032
"Yes, sir."

14
00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.033
"Then tell me that."

15
00:01:26.034 --> 00:01:30.721
"I cannot. I am sick and tired, and I want some water."

16
00:01:30.722 --> 00:01:37.634
He heaved a shuddering sigh, and taking me in his arms, carried me downstairs to the library.

17
00:01:37.635 --> 00:01:47.541
There he brought me a glass of water. Then suddenly overcome with passion, he tried to kiss me, but I turned my face away.

18
00:01:47.542 --> 00:01:58.289
"What's this?" he exclaimed. "You won't kiss the husband of Bertha Mason. Is that right? You consider my arms already filled?"

19
00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:01.137
"At any rate there is no room for me."

20
00:02:01.138 --> 00:02:05.304
"So you intend to live under this roof only as Adele's governess?"

21
00:02:05.305 --> 00:02:08.118
"Adele must have a new governess, sir."

22
00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:15.705
"I have already settled that Adele will go to school, and I don't mean to torment you with hideous recollections of this accursed place.

23
00:02:15.706 --> 00:02:26.345
We won't stay here. I'll give Grace Poole two hundred pounds a year to live here with my wife , as you term that fearful hag who burns people in their beds

24
00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:33.421
and—" "Sir," I interrupted. "You speak of her with such hate, but she cannot help being

25
00:02:33.422 --> 00:02:38.762
insane." "Jane, my darling, it's not because she's insane that I hate

26
00:02:38.763 --> 00:02:42.099
her. If you were insane, do you think I would hate

27
00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.010
you?" "I do

28
00:02:44.011 --> 00:02:48.423
indeed." "Then you know nothing about the sort of love that I am capable

29
00:02:48.424 --> 00:02:59.575
of." I had been struggling with tears because I knew he wouldn't like to see me weep, but now I let my tears flow freely. He tried to pull me to him, but I would have none of

30
00:02:59.576 --> 00:03:06.313
that. "You don't love me then?" he said bitterly. "It was only your status as my wife that you

31
00:03:06.314 --> 00:03:15.642
valued?" "I do love you," I said. "More than ever. But this is the last time I must say that, and I must leave

32
00:03:15.643 --> 00:03:28.785
you." "Leave me? No, no, Jane. I only ask you to endure one more night under this roof, and then we will go to a villa I have in the south of France. You shall be my wife as if I were not married."

33
00:03:28.786 --> 00:03:34.453
I shook my head. "If I lived with you like that, I would be your mistress."

34
00:03:34.454 --> 00:03:45.782
"What a fool I am!" Mr. Rochester cried. "I keep saying that I'm not married, but I forget that you know nothing of that infernal woman or the circumstances of our union."

35
00:03:45.783 --> 00:03:55.694
He began by telling me what I'd already heard from Mrs. Fairfax—that his father didn't want him to be poor when Rowland, his older brother, inherited everything.

36
00:03:55.695 --> 00:04:04.927
Then Rochester said that his father and Rowland arranged for him to marry Bertha Mason, who had a dowry of thirty thousand pounds.

37
00:04:04.928 --> 00:04:15.438
He went to Jamaica and was dazzled by the beautiful Bertha. "I seldom saw her alone, but every man seemed to admire her and envy me.

38
00:04:15.439 --> 00:04:23.358
A marriage took place almost before I knew where I was. I never loved her. I didn't even know her!"

39
00:04:23.359 --> 00:04:34.241
He thought his wife's mother was dead. Only after the wedding did he learn that she was shut up in an insane asylum, as was Bertha's younger brother.

40
00:04:34.242 --> 00:04:42.403
"My father and Rowland knew all this but thought only of Bertha's dowry. I lived with her for four years.

41
00:04:42.404 --> 00:04:55.078
I will spare you the abominable details except to say that no servant would stay because of the continued outbreaks of her violent temper, and I couldn't divorce her because the doctors had discovered that she was insane."

42
00:04:55.079 --> 00:05:00.475
"I sincerely pity you, sir," I said quietly. "Go on."

43
00:05:00.476 --> 00:05:08.641
One night in Jamaica, Mr. Rochester decided to flee to Europe, where he could live without anyone knowing his past.

44
00:05:08.642 --> 00:05:14.704
He brought Bertha back to Thornfield and left her in the care of Grace Poole.

45
00:05:14.705 --> 00:05:24.216
For ten years he roamed from one country to another. He had three mistresses, including Adele's mother, Celine Varens.

46
00:05:24.217 --> 00:05:28.873
"I now hate to remember the time I spent with those women," he said.

47
00:05:28.874 --> 00:05:37.206
I felt the truth of those words and knew if I became his next mistress, he would one day regard me the same way.

48
00:05:37.207 --> 00:05:48.198
"I was searching for love," he said, "but never found it until one day when I was returning to Thornfield on business. My horse slipped on some ice—"

49
00:05:48.199 --> 00:05:54.270
"Don't talk to me of those days, sir," I interrupted, wiping tears from my eyes.

50
00:05:54.271 --> 00:05:57.852
"All I ask, Jane, is that you promise to be mine."

51
00:05:57.853 --> 00:06:04.511
"Mr. Rochester, I will not be yours." I rose from my chair.

52
00:06:04.512 --> 00:06:13.496
"Oh, Jane! My hope, my love, my life!" He cried out in anguish and a sob escaped his lips.

53
00:06:13.497 --> 00:06:16.611
I kissed his cheek and fled the room.

54
00:06:16.611 --> 00:06:20.425
The next morning I slipped quietly from Thornfield.

55
00:06:20.426 --> 00:06:29.577
I carried a small parcel containing only some clothing, a locket, and a ring. My purse held twenty shillings.

56
00:06:29.578 --> 00:06:39.728
I was weeping wildly as I walked along my solitary way. At any moment I could have turned back and been welcomed by my master, but I pressed on.

57
00:06:39.729 --> 00:06:44.482
When I heard a coach approaching, I turned and signaled it to stop.

58
00:06:44.483 --> 00:06:53.136
I asked the driver where he was going, and he named a faraway place where I was sure Mr. Rochester had no connections.

59
00:06:53.137 --> 00:07:00.164
The fare would cost every shilling I had, but I climbed aboard, and the coach rolled away.

